<item>
  <title>[UNDER CONSTRUCTION] A Non-Local Formulation of Water Waves</title>
  <link>https://sg-bradford.github.io/posts/On_a_new_non_Local_Formulation_of_Water_Waves.html</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 





<section id="introduction" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="introduction">(1) Introduction</h2>
<!-- more -->
<p><strong>(1.1) A new non-local formulation of water waves in three dimensions</strong></p>
<p>We start by defining the domain</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0AD=%5C%7B-%5Cinfty%3Cx_j%3C%5Cinfty,%5Cquad%20j=1,2,%5Cquad%20-h%3Cy%3C%5Ceta(x_1,%20x_2,%20t),%5Cquad%20t%3E0%5C%7D%0A"></p>
<p>The classical gravity water wave problem satisfies</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5CDelta%5Cphi=0%5Cquad%5Ctext%7Bin%20%7DD,%0A"> <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5Cphi_y=0%5Cquad%5Ctext%7Bon%20%7Dy=-h,%0A"> <span id="eq-gravity_wave_problem_3"><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5Ceta_t+%5Cphi_%7Bx_1%7D%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D+%5Cphi_%7Bx_2%7D%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7D=%5Cphi_y%5Cquad%5Ctext%7Bon%20%7Dy=%5Ceta,%0A%5Ctag%7B1%7D"></span> <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5Cphi_t+%5Cfrac%7B1%7D%7B2%7D%7C%5Cnabla%5Cphi%7C%5E2+g%5Ceta=%5Cfrac%7B%5Csigma%7D%7B%5Crho%7D%5Cnabla%5Ccdot%5Cleft(%5Cfrac%7B%5Cnabla%5Ceta%7D%7B%5Csqrt%7B1+%7C%5Cnabla%5Ceta%7C%5E2%7D%7D%5Cright)%5Cquad%5Ctext%7Bon%20%7Dy=%5Ceta.%0A"></p>
<p>We aim to reformulate these equations purely in terms of functions on the free boundary. These functions are <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Ceta(x_1,%20x_2,%20t)"> and <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?q(x_1,%20x_2,%20t):=%5Cphi(x_1,%20x_2,%20%5Ceta(x_1,%20x_2,%20t),%20t)">.</p>
<p>Since Equation&nbsp;1 is satisfied on the free surface, and</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5Cphi_%7Bx_1%7D+%5Cphi_y%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D=q_%7Bx_1%7D,%0A"> <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5Cphi_%7Bx_2%7D+%5Cphi_y%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7D=q_%7Bx_2%7D,%0A"></p>
<p>we can create the linear system</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5Cbegin%7Bbmatrix%7D%0A%20%20%20%20%5Cphi_%7Bx_1%7D%20%5C%5C%0A%20%20%20%20%5Cphi_%7Bx_2%7D%0A%5Cend%7Bbmatrix%7D%0A=%0A%5Cbegin%7Bbmatrix%7D%0A%20%20%20%20-%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D%5E2%20&amp;%20-%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7D%20%5C%5C%0A%20%20%20%20-%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7D%20&amp;%20-%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7D%5E2%0A%5Cend%7Bbmatrix%7D%0A%5Cbegin%7Bbmatrix%7D%0A%20%20%20%20%5Cphi_%7Bx_1%7D%20%5C%5C%0A%20%20%20%20%5Cphi_%7Bx_2%7D%0A%5Cend%7Bbmatrix%7D%0A+%0A%5Cbegin%7Bbmatrix%7D%0A%20%20%20%20q_%7Bx_1%7D-%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D%5Ceta_t%20%5C%5C%0A%20%20%20%20q_%7Bx_2%7D-%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7D%5Ceta_t%0A%5Cend%7Bbmatrix%7D%0A"> <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5Cimplies%0A%5Cbegin%7Bbmatrix%7D%0A%20%20%20%201+%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D%5E2%20&amp;%20%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7D%20%5C%5C%0A%20%20%20%20%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7D%20&amp;%201+%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7D%5E2%0A%5Cend%7Bbmatrix%7D%0A%5Cbegin%7Bbmatrix%7D%0A%20%20%20%20%5Cphi_%7Bx_1%7D%20%5C%5C%0A%20%20%20%20%5Cphi_%7Bx_2%7D%0A%5Cend%7Bbmatrix%7D%0A=%0A%5Cbegin%7Bbmatrix%7D%0A%20%20%20%20q_%7Bx_1%7D-%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D%5Ceta_t%20%5C%5C%0A%20%20%20%20q_%7Bx_2%7D-%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7D%5Ceta_t%0A%5Cend%7Bbmatrix%7D.%0A"></p>
<p>The solution of which is</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5Cphi_%7Bx_1%7D=%5Cfrac%7B(1+%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7D%5E2)q_%7Bx_1%7D-%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7Dq_%7Bx_2%7D-%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D%5Ceta_t%7D%7B1+%7C%5Cnabla%5Ceta%7C%5E2%7D,%0A"> <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5Cphi_%7Bx_2%7D=%5Cfrac%7B(1+%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D%5E2)q_%7Bx_2%7D-%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7Dq_%7Bx_1%7D-%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7D%5Ceta_t%7D%7B1+%7C%5Cnabla%5Ceta%7C%5E2%7D,%0A"> <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5Cphi_y=%5Cfrac%7B%5Ceta_t+%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7Dq_%7Bx_1%7D+%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7Dq_%7Bx_2%7D%7D%7B1+%7C%5Cnabla%5Ceta%7C%5E2%7D.%0A"></p>
<p>At this point, the authors suggest that</p>
<p><span id="eq-sqaure_grad_phi"><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%7C%5Cnabla%5Cphi%7C%5E2=%5Cfrac%7B(1+%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7D%5E2)q_%7Bx_1%7D%5E2+(1+%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D%5E2)q_%7Bx_2%7D%5E2+%5Ceta_t%5E2-2%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7Dq_%7Bx_1%7Dq_%7Bx_2%7D%7D%7B1+%7C%5Cnabla%5Ceta%7C%5E2%7D.%0A%5Ctag%7B2%7D"></span></p>
<p>Rather than deriving Equation&nbsp;2 from scratch, we can more easily verify its validity by showing that <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A%5B1+%7C%5Cnabla%5Ceta%7C%5E2%5D%5Ccdot%5B(1+%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7D%5E2)q_%7Bx_1%7D%5E2+(1+%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D%5E2)q_%7Bx_2%7D%5E2+%5Ceta_t%5E2-2%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7Dq_%7Bx_1%7Dq_%7Bx_2%7D%5D%0A"> <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%0A=%5B(1+%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7D%5E2)q_%7Bx_1%7D-%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7Dq_%7Bx_2%7D-%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D%5Ceta_t%5D%5E2+%5B(1+%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D%5E2)q_%7Bx_2%7D-%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7D%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7Dq_%7Bx_1%7D-%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7D%5Ceta_t%5D%5E2+%5B%5Ceta_t+%5Ceta_%7Bx_1%7Dq_%7Bx_1%7D+%5Ceta_%7Bx_2%7Dq_%7Bx_2%7D%5D%5E2,%0A"></p>
<p>since <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?(1+%7C%5Cnabla%5Ceta%7C%5E2)"> must be a factor in the numerator of <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Cphi_%7Bx_1%7D%5E2+%5Cphi_%7Bx_2%7D%5E2+%5Cphi_y%5E2"> for Equation&nbsp;2 to hold.</p>


</section>

